 "brief": "Knot homology and sheaves on the Hilbert scheme of points on the plane — For each braid β ∈Brn we construct a 2-periodic complex Sβ of quasi-coherent C∗× C∗- equivariant sheaves on the",
 "extended": "**Knot homology and sheaves on the Hilbert scheme of points on the plane**\n\n*ALEXEI OBLOMKOV AND LEV ROZANSKY*\n\n83 pp, 78 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** For each braid β ∈Brn we construct a 2-periodic complex Sβ of quasi-coherent C∗× C∗- equivariant sheaves on the non-commutative nested Hilbert scheme Hilbfree 1,n . We show that the triply graded vector space of the hypercohomology H(Sβ ⊗∧•(B)) with B being tautological vector bundle, is an isotopy invariant of the knot obtained by the closure of β. We also show that the support of cohomology of the complex Sβ is supported on the ordinary nested Hilbert scheme Hilb1,n ⊂Hilbfree 1,n , that allows us to relate the triply graded knot homology to the sheaves on Hilb1,n\n\n**Outline.** Front matter; 1 Introduction; 1.1 Motivation; 1.2 Main result; 1.3 Sheaves on Hilbert schemes; 1.4 Braids and matrix factorizations; 1.5 Structure of the paper; 2 Basic space and Matrix factorizations; 2.1 Notations, conventions; 2.2 Matrix factorizations: three lemmas; 2.3 Koszul matrix factorizations; 3 Equivariant structure of matrix factorizatio; 3.1 Technical lemmas: non-equivariant version; 3.2 Push forward; 3.3 Chevalley-Eilenberg complex; 3.4 Equivariant matrix factorizations; 3.5 Extension lemmas; 3.6 Lifting lemma for morphisms",
